{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111671","id":2916318943,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6t037f","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111671","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111671.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111671.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111671","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111671/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111671/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111671/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/762e8b664d5a2fb09b85695af1e807381c090a84","number":111671,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix `AnimatableBody2D` cannot move with parent when `sync_to_physics=true`","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/54915*\r\n- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/58269*\r\n- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/63140*\r\n- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/76685*\r\n- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82373*\r\n- *https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98970*\r\n\r\nIt is not a easy issue. I create this PR for giving a demo to discuss how to solve this issue.\r\n\r\nThis MRP comes from #58269 , updated to 4.5 version.\r\n[AnimatableBodyTest45.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22921186/AnimatableBodyTest45.zip)\r\n\r\n**Issue Description**\r\n\r\nThere are three scenarios about this issue.\r\n\r\n- Using AnimationPlayer to play an animation. e.g. an moving platform.\r\n- PathFollow. e.g. moving follows a curve path.\r\n- Collission. e.g. carry a box with platform and move. **NO JITTER**\r\n\r\n**Investigation**\r\n\r\nCurrent `AnimationBody2D` is `StaticBody2D`, it supports collision. And `AnimationPlayer` can modify the the position of `AnimationBody2D` or its parent node.\r\n\r\nWhen `sync_to_physics=true` by default, the hack operation is listen a `NOTIFICATION_LOCAL_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` which means current node transform had been updated. It is a specific event, considering it occur only once. When current node position update, `AnimatableBody2D` first update the position to `PhysicsServer`, and revert to position before update, then listen to `PhysicsServer` to callback after collision. I think this might be more accurate for `PhysicsServer` to compute the final position of `StaticBody2D`?\r\n\r\nHere we cannot use `NOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED`, as this events occurs more than once. If we used it to update `PhysicsServer` then revert. The next event will re-send the reverted position to `PhysicsServer` again.\r\n\r\nBut without `NOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED`, the child node cannot get when parent node moved, and cannot update the position of PhysicsServer. That causes collision broken.\r\n\r\n**Solution**\r\n\r\nFirst, we need a new notification to notice child nodes when their parent moved. This event should be triggered only once, likes `NOTIFICATION_LOCAL_TRANSFORM_CHANGED`. I created a `NOTIFICATION_PARENT_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` and noticed it in `canvas_item`.\r\n\r\nSecond, listen `NOTIFICATION_PARENT_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` in `AnimatableBody2D` as `NOTIFICATION_LOCAL_TRANSFORM_CHANGED`, and only with `sync_to_physics=true` to prevent it freeze node when `sync_to_physics=false`.\r\n\r\nThird, there are still some JITTER, I find it caused by the PhysicsServer callback didn't always be invoked before every `process` iteration, so add additional `PhysicsServer2D::get_singleton()->flush_queries();` in `main.cpp`.\r\n\r\n**Etc**\r\n\r\nIn MRP, I cannot find out the different from `sync_to_physics=true` to `sync_to_physics=false`, Why we need `sync_to_physics=true`? Is there any scenario that `sync_to_physics=false` cannot handle?\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull reque